15 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows the CueO-MacHis amino acid sequence with different segments color-coded in black, blue, orange, green, and red. Panel B is a diagram of genetic constructs for expressing CueO-MacHis and DsRed in the cytosol, chloroplast, endoplasmic reticulum \(ER\), and apoplast, each labeled with genetic elements such as p35s, CHS, TP, SP, ER, and t35s.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Figure shows protein expression and degradation analysis in two panels. Panel A contains a Western blot and a bar chart analyzing DsRed and CueO-MacHis compartment localization, indicating cytosolic DsRed and CueO-MacHis enrichment in chloroplasts. Panel B presents Western blots showing CueO-MacHis stability under various extraction conditions and incubation times, with and without protease inhibitors or copper sulfate, alongside a bar chart quantifying CueO-MachIs integrity across treatments.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a bar chart of CueO-MacHis protein yield increasing with Agrobacteria OD600 and a corresponding protein gel indicating CueO-MacHis expression at varying Agrobacteria densities. Panel B presents a bar chart of protein yield increasing with days post infiltration, with a Western blot showing CueO-MacHis expression over time. Panel C displays a bar chart of protein yield decreasing with older plant age, paired with a Western blot indicating CueO-MacHis expression in plants aged two to eight weeks.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Three-dimensional surface plot shows CueO-MacHis yield as a function of plant age and harvest date, alongside a statistical table summarizing significant quadratic model factors, coefficients of determination, and p-values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a 3D surface plot and statistical table for TSP reduction, modeled with a reduced cubic model; significant p-values for temperature and pH effects are reported. Panel B shows a 3D surface plot and statistical summary for CueO yield using a reduced linear model; pH is highly significant. Panel C displays a 3D response surface and model statistics for CueO-to-TSP purity, employing a reduced quadratic model, with temperature and pH both significant predictors.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
